    {
      "title": "Hi-tech Shenzhen takes centre stage as Xi sends ‘Chinamaxxing’ message at Apec summit",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/hi-tech-shenzhen-chinamaxxing-xi-apec-summit",
      "description": "<p>Host city offers showcase of China’s rise into a confident and innovative power central to global economy</p><p>In a Shenzhen square on a balmy evening, locals and tourists watched the dozens of glinting towers that make up the city’s skyline ripple through the colour spectrum – cyan and violet, cyber green, China’s national scarlet and gold – repeatedly flashing the words “Apec 2026”.</p><p>The Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit is a dream showcase for one of China’s most advanced cities, and the country’s leader, Xi Jinping, is basking in its neon glow.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/hi-tech-shenzhen-chinamaxxing-xi-apec-summit\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T11:18:26"
